hexagon: read the slot index of a fused recurrent op before the graph goes to the DSP
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-fusion/0004-hexagon-htp-gdn-slot-index-from-host-and-error-report.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

Finding gdn-slot-stale of fuzz-hexhost, task #126. The fused recurrent ops
GDN_CONV_STEP, GDN_CONV_CHUNK and GDN_STATE_STEP get the row of the state
table from the s_copy input. The host read s_copy in enqueue_op, when it put
the op into a batch. At that time the value can be incorrect in two
conditions:

- ggml-alloc gives the bytes of s_copy to a different tensor after the last
  reader of s_copy in the node order. An op of an earlier batch of the same
  graph writes that tensor on the DSP before the host puts the fused op into
  its batch.
- s_copy is the output of an op of the graph (for example a GET_ROWS of an
  index table), not an input. The DSP did not run that op yet.

With an incorrect value, the fused op reads and writes an incorrect row of
the state table. When the value is not a row, the host runs the unfused ops.

This patch reads the index of each fused recurrent op in graph_compute before
the first op of the graph goes to the DSP (latch_gdn_slots), and enqueue_op
uses that value. The matcher does not fuse a chain whose s_copy is not an
input of the graph. A replay of the batch cache reads s_copy at its start,
before an op of the graph goes to the DSP.

Evidence (2026-09-23):
- The regression inputs tests/fuzz/hexhost/regress/graph/gdn-slot-stale-
  computed.bin and gdn-slot-stale-reuse.bin give the finding before this
  patch in the none, asan and ubsan builds, debug and release. With the
  five patches of fuzz-hexhost they give no finding in the asan build, debug
  and release.
- The graph fuzzer with the condition on ran for 10 minutes with this patch
  (14852 executions): no finding.
- With the five patches of fuzz-hexhost, the corpora of the campaign (549
  graph, 2468 kparams, 1745 dirty, 609 repack and 695 envparse inputs) give no
  finding in the asan build, debug and release. The open findings of tasks
  #157 and #158 stay off in that run.
- The phone (OnePlus 13, HTP0 v79): one graph input of the fuzz corpus gives
  "the s_copy index is not a row of the state table (index 1057826292,
  1 slots)" with the libraries before this patch, and then "GGML ABORT
  dspqueue_read failed: 0x0000002e". With the libraries of the five patches
  the same input gives no abort.
- The fused ops of the Qwen3.5 graphs are the same before and after (x86,
  the real-graph tool of fuzz-hexhost with the fake DSP): 2B decode 18
  GDN_CONV_STEP and 18 GDN_STATE_STEP, 2B prefill 18 GDN_CONV_CHUNK, 4B
  decode 24 and 24, 4B prefill 24.
- The phone check of the five patches of fuzz-hexhost together (OnePlus 13,
  the 2B Q8_0 on HTP0, thermal status 0, cpu7 cap 4.32 GHz, battery 27.6 to
  27.7 °C, MemAvailable 8.9 to 9.5 GB):
  - test-backend-ops on HTP0 in five op groups (GATED_DELTA_NET and
    SSM_CONV, MUL_MAT_ID, CONCAT CPY GET_ROWS SET_ROWS, the binary ops with
    GLU and SOFT_MAX, NORM RMS_NORM SCALE): each group passes before and
    after.
  - llama-bench tg32 -r 3 after one warmup at 23.76 t/s: before 23.56 ±
    0.10, after 23.59 ± 0.27, before 23.63 ± 0.13, after 23.57 ± 0.11 t/s.
  - llama-speculative-simple with the MTP draft of depth 4, temperature 0,
    64 tokens: before 23.589 and 23.685 t/s, after 24.076 and 24.029 t/s.
    Each run accepts 44 drafts (52.381 %), and the four runs give the same
    text.
  - The graph driver of fuzz-hexhost (HTP0 against the CPU of the phone, 40
    random graph inputs): 17 inputs differ before, and 15 after, all in the
